# No iframe shells (except specific cases)

Default UX is **in-page native UI** — React routes, native dropdown panels, dialogs, and full navigations. Do **not** wrap primary product surfaces in iframes, Simple Browser embeds, nested browsing contexts, or “app-in-an-app” shells.

## Prefer

- Native `<nav>` dropdowns with **logical section groups** (labeled clusters), click/hover + Escape + outside-click
- Direct React Router links and in-app pages
- Modals/dialogs for focused tasks (e.g. View as role)
- Opening external documents with the **system viewer** or a real download — not an embedded PDF/HTML iframe chrome inside the IDE or product

## Allowed iframe exceptions (only these)

- **Payment / identity vendors** that require hosted fields (e.g. Stripe Elements card iframe)
- **Explicit third-party embeds** the product must show (maps, approved video players) when a native alternative is unavailable
- Document the exception in code comments when added

## Do not

- Use iframes for primary navigation, admin menus, dashboards, or document galleries
- Open product previews inside Cursor Simple Browser / iframe panels as the default agent workflow — open files in the editor or system apps instead
- Ship mega-menus as one undifferentiated flat list when domains differ (group Operations / People / Content / Catalog, etc.)

